# Backend conventions

Single project `PMS.API`. Namespaces match folders. One business module at a time under `Modules/<Name>/`:

`Controllers/` `DTOs/` `Models/` `Services/` `Validators/` (`Mappings/` if needed)

Register new services in `Configuration/DependencyInjectionExtensions.cs`. Add `DbSet` + `IEntityTypeConfiguration`. Physical names use a module schema from `DbSchemas` and a prefix: `mst_` catalogs, `tbl_` business tables, `log_` activity or audit rows, `vw_` views, `fnc_` functions. Entities inherit `BaseEntity`. New tables = EF migration, never hand-edit snapshots unless required.

## API

- Routes: `/api/v1/...`. Auth required unless `[AllowAnonymous]`.
- Guard with `[RequirePermission(Permissions.X)]` from `Shared/Constants/Permissions.cs`.
- Return `ApiResponse<T>` / `PagedResult<T>`. 404 uses `Fail("NOT_FOUND", ...)`.
- Validate with FluentValidation (assembly-scanned). JSON enums as strings.
- Pagination: `page` >= 1, `perPage` clamp 1–100.

## Follow existing modules

Copy patterns from `Modules/Customers` and `Modules/Resources`. Integration tests: `tests/PMS.IntegrationTests/`. Dev bypass is Development-only — do not ship it as real auth.
